00:14:00.845 --> 00:14:02.125
>> So

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:08.250
to answer that, here's what I would say.

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:13.450
Work on the basin is relatively minor.

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:19.690
We've said right off the bat that public works will deliver three new basin tops.

00:14:20.695 --> 00:14:30.455
And the reason we do that is anytime you reclaim a road, you know, you end up with a product that lasts a solid 30. It will need maintenance,

00:14:30.855 --> 00:14:37.720
but the underlying structure of the repair is good for at least thirty years. So, there's never a reason to reclaim

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:40.280
without replacing the basin tops,

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.560
because the basin tops aren't going to go another thirty years.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:47.320
So, they were originally going to supply one,

00:14:47.785 --> 00:14:52.025
and what we've said is we'll supply three because there's only three there.

00:14:52.265 --> 00:14:54.345
So, we'll supply all of them.

00:14:54.825 --> 00:15:00.105
So, it's not it won't be a big reduction in their expense, but it'll be a slight reduction

00:15:00.825 --> 00:15:02.025
in their expense.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:06.590
They will have a little bit of labor in remortering

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:08.910
the pipe that goes into

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:12.510
or actually comes out of the one basin,

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:14.990
which was the cause of the sinkhole

00:15:15.475 --> 00:15:18.355
that occurred in that parking lot before.

00:15:18.675 --> 00:15:20.915
So that shouldn't be a big deal.

00:15:21.315 --> 00:15:24.435
I believe the quote already had

00:15:24.675 --> 00:15:26.355
in the cost

00:15:27.475 --> 00:15:29.315
for the additional

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:31.340
