And the town has basically said, we'll pay

00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:41.820
for

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:44.060
the materials testing lab,

00:15:44.635 --> 00:15:47.035
as well as the proctor

00:15:47.195 --> 00:15:49.195
and the guy monitoring.

00:15:49.355 --> 00:15:49.995
So,

00:15:50.635 --> 00:16:00.075
and we'll handle backfilling behind the curbing at the completion of the job, which was not part of the original quote anyway, because most paving contractors contractors

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:03.000
don't ever really do that,

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:05.800
and you have to do it afterward.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:14.040
So there shouldn't be anything, if there's any increase in costs, it will be the fact that the town ordinarily

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:14.760
requires

00:16:15.345 --> 00:16:16.625
the contractors

00:16:16.625 --> 00:16:19.745
to get an actual performance bond for the job.

00:16:20.705 --> 00:16:25.425
And that is because the town doesn't want to get caught holding the bag

00:16:25.665 --> 00:16:30.750
if they do something bad. And a performance bond just essentially guarantees

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:41.310
that if there's something major wrong with the work, you know, you essentially have some way to file an insurance claim. So those are really the things,

00:16:43.435 --> 00:16:45.195
you know, I don't know what

00:16:45.515 --> 00:16:48.555
the cost of that is. It's not zero,

00:16:48.955 --> 00:16:53.515
but it's an ordinary thing done with paving projects.

00:16:53.915 --> 00:16:58.010
The other thing I would mention is that there is $8,000

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:01.290
sitting in the AES Capital Fund.

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:04.730
So, if you had an overage,

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:07.290
you know, less than $8,000

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:10.650
you would simply pay for it out of the existing money

00:17:10.795 --> 00:17:13.435
that is already in the fund.

00:17:14.235 --> 00:17:16.955
The other thing that's possible to bite you,

00:17:17.195 --> 00:17:19.035
but doesn't look like it will,

00:17:19.355 --> 00:17:23.195
is all of these contracts have an asphalt escalation

00:17:23.195 --> 00:17:24.635
factor built into them.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:28.720
That is based on the cost of liquid asphalt

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:31.120
on the week the job is done.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:43.385
And all the contractors put that in there because the reality is asphalt's commodity and the price of it goes up and down. And the contractors don't want to get caught holding the bag.

00:17:43.865 --> 00:17:44.425
You

